caption: <$refresh>
title: $:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/docs/api/widgets/refresh

! Introduction
The `<$refresh>` widget (JS module `$:/plugins/yan/hypergsd/modules/widgets/refresh.js`) freezes its children against TiddlyWiki's default refresh: they only re-render when a tiddler matching the `subfilter` whitelist changes. This is the plugin's core performance architecture — dashboards stay invisible to the CPU until a GSD item actually changes.

The subfilter is evaluated with the widget as filter context, so whitelists can reference `<currentTiddler>`.

! Content and Attributes

|!Attribute |!Description |
|subfilter |Filter whose output is the whitelist of "interesting" changed titles |
|''any other attribute'' |Any additional attribute acts as a ''buster'': if its value changes between renders, the widget re-renders itself (`refreshSelf`) regardless of the whitelist |

! Whitelist authoring rules

* Prefix and tag runs only — a literal `[[title]]` run emits its title unconditionally and defeats the gate.
* Only one `:and` chain per filter; additional scoping uses subtraction runs (`-[…]`).
* Reusable runs: `[subfilter<hgsd-type-gate>]` (items of any type in the Type tag list). The type gate is draft-immune (a draft inherits the base tiddler's tags, so without the exclusion every keystroke in an open editor opened every gate carrying the run).

! Example
```
<$refresh subfilter="[subfilter<hgsd-type-gate>] [prefix[$:/config/hypergsd]] -[is[draft]]" hgsd-filter-buster=<<item-titles>>>
    …frozen content…
</$refresh>
```